(BAS-39 - rule 1: a period closes the MOST RECENTLY OPENED clause, and
 only that one. Three clauses are open when the innermost `if` ends; its
 single period closes the innermost `if` alone, so `print "still inside"`
 is still inside the middle `if` (true) and the outer `if` (true) and runs.
 Also covers: BAS-40 (one period closes one level) - the two extra periods
 on the last statement are what finally get back to the top level.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-39.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   innermost
   still inside
   back at the top
)
a number called n is 1.
If n is equal to 1 then,
    If n is equal to 1 then,
        If n is equal to 1 then, print "innermost".
        print "still inside"...
print "back at the top".
